From: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:49:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(remote): cover the remaining patch lines on the SSH
 recovery runner

Codecov reports 18 uncovered changed lines on PR #68 at 94.59% patch
coverage. Add regression cases for the paths the existing suite reaches
only with an injected transport or not at all:

- the fetch's own required-output error, a durable cancel request at
  reattachment, cleanup of a retained attempt behind a verified receipt,
  and a stale-attempt sweep that refuses;
- the transport the runner owns and closes itself, including both
  superseded-journal branches, using a refusing ssh/scp on PATH;
- phylogeny's local and remote log/key branch in run_workflow;
- the shared single-quote escaping in verify_remote_sizes.

The three Codex findings are already fixed at 5115109; these tests pin
the uncovered parts of those fixes and of the recovery protocol.

Co-authored-by: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <6759885+hyperpolymath@users.noreply.github.com>
